# Spec Review: www_products_photos_20261115

## Round 2

### What this track proposes
The track restores real photos on the www products page at every viewport width and stops a repeat with tests. It fixes what is still wrong at HEAD: the text box that covers the blended-learning photo, the missing Tutor section picture, the squeezed pictures at 1024 px, and the covered home hero. It adds a Playwright e2e (each photo loaded, visible, at most 30 percent covered, with a 100 px short side and a 5 percent aspect assertion, at 390, 980, 1024, and 1280 px, in en and th), a HeroSection unit test, and it runs the e2e twice: in the ci.yml affected job and in the www CD workflow before the deploy step, so a failing e2e stops the deploy.

### How the current system works, per this spec
Commit 8193625ca already removed the hidden xl:block wrapper from the products hero and added 8 product pictures, and those load at all four widths. The services/blended-learning photo stays covered by the See How We Report Results overlay, the Tutor section has no picture, and the home hero photo is 40 percent covered at 390 px. The ci.yml affected job builds, lints, type-checks, and tests www-reading-advantage but runs no e2e; the www CD deploys on push and needs only its own select job. The ci.yml job Build, Lint, and Test is red on master for an unrelated architecture-check cause, so the e2e gate goes into the CD job itself rather than a CD-needs-CI link.

### Findings
- F5 [Nit] spec.md AC-3(b) and plan.md Runner facts part (b): the start command is an open "or" — "next start -p 3123 or node .next/standalone/server.js". Rationale: the standalone output does not include public/ or .next/static, so the server.js option needs a copy step the plan does not name, and a naive pick fails the e2e for a reason Red did not choose. The app builds standalone output (next.config.ts line 17), so both options work, but only next start needs no extra step. Name next start -p 3123 as the command and drop the alternative.

